<title>GERMANY: German minister says to cull British, Swiss cattle.</title>
<headline>German minister says to cull British, Swiss cattle.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A senior German Agriculture Ministry official said on Wednesday all cattle imported from Britain and Switzerland would be culled to calm public fears after a case of mad cow disease in a Germany.</p>
<p>The state secretary at the ministry Franz-Josef Feiter told a news conference the decision would affect 2,600 cattle from Britain and a further 2,600 from Switzerland.</p>
